            <ArticleTitle>Evidence-based practice part 1: pain definitions, pathophysiologic mechanisms, and theories.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>357-65</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Evidence-based practice consists of using research evidence to validate patient care. A body of evidence exists on pain mechanisms and pain management; however, patients continue to experience unrelieved pain. This 3-part series on pain will explore evidence in pain theories, pathophysiological mechanisms, instruments to measure pain, and how to manage pain in PACU patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
